    "body": "## Summary\n\n```diff\n-transliterate('ýÝ ẞ ᴀ ₐ ①')                    // 'yU    '\n+transliterate('ýÝ ẞ ᴀ ₐ ①')                    // 'yY SS A a 1'\n-transliterate('ъ', { unknown: '?' })            // '?'\n+transliterate('ъ', { unknown: '?' })            // ''\n-slugify('Hello World', { allowedChars: undefined }) // 'e-d'\n+slugify('Hello World', { allowedChars: undefined }) // 'hello-world'\n-slugify('2022年中文01英文nihao02')               // '2022nian-zhong-wen-01ying-wen-nihao02'\n+slugify('2022年中文01英文nihao02')               // '2022-nian-zhong-wen-01-ying-wen-nihao-02'\n```\n\nFixes #107, #246, #256 and #239. Applies the nullish `allowedChars` fallback proposed in #252, preserving explicit empty strings. Corrected mappings are included in full and Latin exports. The generator now preserves known-empty mappings through lookup, map population and resets.\n\nThe Latin selector includes existing mappings for Latin characters outside the original three blocks and numbers whose compatibility decomposition contains ASCII digits. It remains separate from the full language data.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- **Before:** the new regression cases failed on the existing source; the published 2.6.2 reproduction recorded 24 failing assertions across Node, browser UMD and browser ESM for the four focused bug references.\n  **After:** 96 source tests and 14 built-package tests pass, including all reported characters and #239's complete example, ignored spans, custom deletions and resets.\n- `bun run test:coverage`: 100% function coverage; 99.55% statements and 96.07% branches.\n- Built-package tests also pass on the minimum Node 20.0.0 and current Node 20 runtimes.\n- TypeScript `tsc --noEmit`, lint of all tracked applicable files, and `git diff --check` pass. Regenerating all 135 data files produces identical bytes.\n- Latin JavaScript artifacts remain below the existing 20,000-byte guard: Node 17,984 bytes, UMD 18,209 bytes, ESM 17,504 bytes.\n\n## Merge Danger\n\n**Door:** Two-way\n\nThe commit can be reverted; package version remains 2.6.2, with changes recorded under Unreleased.\n\n**Blast Radius:** Output\n\nDefault mixed Chinese/Latin/numeric slug boundaries change. `fixChineseSpacing: false` disables inserted boundaries. Explicit empty mappings remain silent when `unknown` is set. The Latin repertoire expands and its minified, uncompressed size increases from about 10 KB to about 18 KB. README and type documentation describe these changes.\n",
